title: "From Attachment to Emotion-Like Control: An AI-Assisted Exploratory Computational Study of Value, Memory, Prediction Error, Self-Models, and Body-State Feedback"
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fukuoka"
    given-names: "Shinobu"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fukuoka1980521-beep/emotion-control-systems-exploration"
url: "https://github.com/fukuoka1980521-beep/emotion-control-systems-exploration"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22780290"
abstract: >-
  Exploratory computational experiments examining whether emotion-like functional patterns can arise from combinations of value, attachment, memory, prediction error, agent identity, self-models, and body-state feedback. The work explicitly distinguishes functional emotion-like behavior from subjective feeling and preserves negative findings, design failures, and corrective experiments.
keywords:
  - computational emotion
  - affective computing
  - reinforcement learning
  - appraisal
  - attachment
  - prediction error
  - self-model
  - interoception
  - emotion-like behavior
